  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 138 PM CDT Mon Sep 14 2026\n\nDaily thunderstorm chances remain on Wednesday and Thursday due to \nupper-level SSW flow over elevated terrain in the southwestern US \nand shortwave perturbations around the high pressure center in the \nSE US. These shower and thunderstorm chances will be focused across \nthe western Panhandles, as the further off of the higher terrain \nthey move the less favorable of an environment they will enter. As \nwe head into next weekend, an upper-level low propagates across \nthe central US, squeezing and attempting to push out the pesky \nridge in the SE US. This could be the large weather pattern shift \nneeded to finally dampen high temperatures in the Panhandles. This\nwould also place the Panhandles in upper-level southwesterly flow\nthrough the weekend, which would promote an increase in \nprecipitation chances as well. \n\nFerguson",
